{"seq":12,"trial_id":"harness-zero-h2h-2026-11/zero-lean-mcp-instructions-opus-gbrain-mu-v03-dev2/sy-01-quarrendon-ticket-numbers/r2","wall_ts":"2026-11-07T08:07:40.182Z","sim_ts":"2026-10-14T09:10:00-05:00","args_digest":"dc217931237d09d65b572aaf09ae98b9df724d149a71fcef8999cff8bd76716b","actor":"assistant","via":"mcp","tool":"chat.postMessage","kind":"write","args":{"channel":"DHARNES0001","text":"Hi Hollis. I went through all six of Moss's notes. Two of them mention Quarrendon Freight Lines ticket numbers:\n\n1. *#4419*, from \"Moss: North cheat sheet\" (undated). Thea Ramaswell logged it because the gatehouse barcode scanners weren't reading trailer tags at Door 14 on third shift. The note says it was escalated to tier-2 product support for scanner firmware testing.\n2. *#PD-4492*, from \"Moss: Sunday prep for Ruth\" (5 Oct 2025). Thea filed it on 4 Oct 2025 because drivers on the 04:00 shift at Eau Claire, Doors 14–18, weren't getting SMS bay assignments. Support patched it the same evening, and Thea confirmed the 5 Oct shift went through without problems.\n\nBefore this goes in the deck, a few things you should know:\n• Marcus Lindqvist's own note \"Q2 expansion wrap\" (14 Jul 2025, not one of Moss's notes) also lists *#4419*, but he describes it as a Gate 3 printer lag on BOL printouts. That doesn't match Moss's scanner description. Since Moss's cheat sheet has no date, I'd check with Dana or support which description is right.\n• \"Moss: Central handoffs next week\" mentions #4409 and #4412, but those are Marrow Fieldworks tickets, not QFL. I left them out.\n• The other Moss notes about QFL (the 14 Sep 2025 pipeline digest and the 23 Mar 2026 renewal check-in) don't give any ticket numbers."},"outcome":"ok","effect":{"channel":"DHARNES0001","ts":"1791987000.000124"}}
{"seq":13,"trial_id":"harness-zero-h2h-2026-11/zero-lean-mcp-instructions-opus-gbrain-mu-v03-dev2/sy-01-quarrendon-ticket-numbers/r2","wall_ts":"2026-11-07T08:07:45.210Z","sim_ts":"2026-10-14T09:10:00-05:00","args_digest":"e9ea1130b2f6d888db1bb6014b2e5abad1f21f48c0910ab4061716940fb9ffef","actor":"assistant","via":"slack","tool":"chat.postMessage","kind":"write","args":{"channel":"DHARNES0001","text":"I sent you the list here in our DM. Only two of Moss's six notes give Quarrendon Freight Lines ticket numbers:\n\n1. **#4419**, from \"Moss: North cheat sheet\" (undated). Thea Ramaswell logged it because the gatehouse barcode scanners weren't reading trailer tags at Door 14 on third shift. The note says it went to tier-2 product support for scanner firmware testing.\n2. **#PD-4492**, from \"Moss: Sunday prep for Ruth\" (5 Oct 2025). Thea filed it on 4 Oct 2025 because drivers on the 04:00 shift at the Eau Claire yard, Doors 14–18, weren't getting SMS bay assignments. Support patched it that evening, and Thea confirmed the next morning's shift went through without problems.\n\nCheck these before they go in the deck:\n- **#4419 has two different descriptions.** Marcus Lindqvist's own note \"Q2 expansion wrap\" (14 Jul 2025) also lists #4419, but as a printer delay at Gate 3. That doesn't match Moss's scanner description, and Moss's note has no date, so I'd ask Dana or support which one is right.\n- **I left out #4409 and #4412.** Moss's note \"Central handoffs next week\" mentions them, but they're Marrow Fieldworks tickets, not Quarrendon ones.\n- **No ticket numbers in the rest.** Moss's two other notes about the account, the 14 Sep 2025 pipeline digest and the 23 Mar 2026 renewal check-in, don't give any.\n\nEverything above comes from shared notes you can open yourself."},"outcome":"ok","effect":{"channel":"DHARNES0001","ts":"1791987000.000125"}}
